      {
        "name": "elongation",
        "number": 1,
        "text": "Find the difference: (Moon's longitude - Sun's longitude). Add 360 degrees if the result is negative. The result will be between 0 and 360 degrees and will show how advanced Moon is with respect to Sun."
      },
      {
        "name": "completed",
        "number": 2,
        "text": "Divide this result by 12 degrees. Ignore the remainder and take the quotient."
      },
      {
        "name": "index",
        "number": 3,
        "text": "Add 1 to the quotient. You get a number from 1 to 30. That will give the index of the tithi running."
      },
      {
        "name": "name",
        "number": 4,
        "text": "Refer to Table 3 and find the name of the tithi. There are 15 tithis and the same tithis repeat in the brigher and darker fortnights."
